<section class="public-page-hero policy-hero"><span class="section-kicker">YOUR INFORMATION MATTERS</span><h1>Privacy<br />policy.</h1><p>What HealthTrack stores, how it is used, and the choices available to you.</p><span class="policy-date">Last updated: 23 October 2026 · Local demonstration edition</span></section>
<div class="policy-layout public-section"><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Privacy sections"><a href="#privacy-scope">This installation</a><a href="#privacy-information">Information stored</a><a href="#privacy-purpose">How it is used</a><a href="#privacy-access">Who has access</a><a href="#privacy-storage">Storage & retention</a><a href="#privacy-cookies">Cookies & preferences</a><a href="#privacy-choices">Your choices</a><a href="#privacy-contact">Contact</a></nav><article class="policy-content">
<section id="privacy-scope"><h2>1. This installation</h2><p>This notice describes the current local demonstration of HealthTrack, a fitness tracking and coordination application. The operator is the person or organization that supplied your access to this installation. Demo accounts contain fictional information.</p><p>This installation is not intended for real sensitive health records. Contact the operator before using it with personal health information outside the demonstration.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-information"><h2>2. Information stored</h2><ul><li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> name, email address, password hash, role, optional biography, timezone and reminder preferences.</li><li><strong>Health and activity:</strong> measurements, workouts, meals, water amounts, sleep start/wake times and notes you enter; optional personal targets, dashboard focus and saved-entry preferences.</li><li><strong>Guidance and coordination:</strong> trainer assignments, plans, feedback, appointments and appointment purposes.</li><li><strong>Contact enquiries:</strong> the name, email address, subject and message you submit, when it arrived and whether the administrator has handled it.</li><li><strong>Application activity:</strong> in-app notifications, account status, audit events and operational diagnostic logs.</li></ul><p>Trainers can add plans and feedback for their currently assigned clients. Administrators maintain assignments and the healthcare professional directory. Passwords are stored as hashes, rather than readable passwords.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-purpose"><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>HealthTrack uses this information to authenticate accounts, show personal records and progress charts, provide trainer guidance, coordinate appointments, generate in-app reminders and enforce account permissions.</p><p>Administrators can view aggregate usage and an activity audit to manage the installation. Contact form submissions are used by administrators to review and follow up on your enquiry. The application does not include advertising, marketing trackers or an external analytics integration.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-access"><h2>4. Who can access information</h2><ul><li><strong>Clients:</strong> their own logs, profile, published plans, feedback, appointments and notifications.</li><li><strong>Currently assigned trainers:</strong> assigned-client profiles and progress, plus the plans, feedback and trainer appointments they manage.</li><li><strong>Administrators:</strong> account and assignment management, the professional directory, aggregate reports, contact enquiries and professional-booking coordination. Application permissions do not grant them access to raw client health-log or progress pages.</li></ul><p>Appointment purposes are visible to the responsible trainer or administrative professional-booking coordinator. The operator and anyone with sufficient access to the host computer or database may be able to access stored data independently of the application's page permissions.</p><p>No external email or SMS delivery is enabled. Development password reset messages are saved to a private local folder for the operator's demonstration workflow; they are not emailed.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-storage"><h2>5. Storage, security and retention</h2><p>Records are stored in the installation's SQL Server LocalDB database. HTTPS protects browser connections. Health measurements, activity quantities, water amounts, personal targets and notes, plan guidance, trainer feedback, appointment notes, profile biographies and contact enquiry details are encrypted before storage. Encryption keys are protected by the Windows account running this installation.</p><p>This is field encryption, not encryption of the entire database or its backups. Account identity, ownership references, dates (including sleep times), routine categories, focus/display preferences and activity metadata remain available to the application. Anyone with sufficient access to the running host account may still access decrypted information. The operator manages storage protection and backups separately.</p><p>Contact enquiries remain in the database until the operator removes them; marking a message as handled does not delete it. There is no automatic retention or account-erasure schedule in this demonstration. Records remain until deleted through supported application actions or removed by the operator. Account deactivation disables access but does not erase records. Audit events may retain action and record identifiers after a log is deleted; they do not contain snapshots of its health values.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-cookies"><h2>6. Cookies and local preferences</h2><p>The application uses cookies for sign-in, request-forgery protection and temporary status messages. Choosing Remember me can keep a sign-in cookie between browser sessions. Signing out ends the active sign-in session.</p><p>The browser also stores your sidebar-collapse preference in local storage. You can clear site data through your browser settings; this can sign you out and reset preferences. Fonts, icons and page imagery are served from this installation rather than third-party content services.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-choices"><h2>7. Your choices</h2><p>You can correct or delete your own health logs, edit profile information and change reminder preferences in Settings. Goals & preferences lets you change optional targets and visible cards without deleting records. My progress lets you download a CSV report for your selected period; Wellness trends also exports seven-day summaries. Trainers can export reports for current assigned clients; administrators can export de-identified activity summaries. These reports are not complete account archives. Contact the operator about account deactivation, full access or erasure requests. Automated complete account export and erasure are not implemented.</p><p>For questions about what your trainer can see, your assignment or a record you cannot change, contact the operator who provided your access.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-contact"><h2>8. Questions and changes</h2><p>Visit <a href="/Home/Contact">Contact us</a> for the available support details. This page will carry an updated date when its content changes. Before public production use, the operator needs to provide its identity, contact details and policies applicable to that deployment.</p></section>
</article></div>
